    "q-214240": {
      "dom_id": "step-q214240",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Which of the following are equivalence relations on $P(N)?$\n\nI. $|A|=|B|$\n\nII. $A⊆B$\n\nIII. $A⊂B$",
      "worked_solution": "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nWith this in mind, let's consider each of the given relations.\n\n- The relation \"$=$\" for the cardinalities of sets is an equivalence relation since it's reflexive, symmetric, and transitive.\n\n- The relation \"$⊆$\" is not an equivalence relation. For example, it is not symmetric since $\\{1\\}⊆\\{1,2\\}$ but $\\{1,2\\}⊈\\{1\\}.$\n\n- The relation \"$⊂$\" is not an equivalence relation. For example, it is not reflexive since $N⊄N.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
